{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1451793-can-t-find-reference-any-way-to-get-rid-of-nightmare-dice-in-c20","id":1451793,"title":"Can't find reference, any way to get rid of Nightmare Dice in C20?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-11T19:19:58-07:00","id":1451793,"title":"Can't find reference, any way to get rid of Nightmare Dice in C20?","content":"I might just be missing the reference, but it seems a bit inhibiting to play a fun Unleashing or even just a cantrip for the trivial reasons often given in the examples (i.e., a satyr siccing gremlins on the office computers to have a day off, a childling flying off bored from the playground) ...when any botch can set your character irreversibly on a downward slide towards Bedlam from accruing Nightmare Dice that will sit there in your dice pool looking sinister and reminding you not to cast any frivolous cantrips if you value a long-term character. (And with a smaller dice pool, like 3 or 4 dice, a botch seems pretty likely, in fact.)<br /> <br /> I'm not referring to waiting until you get enough of them to get a cursed Willpower point that will bedevil a character permanently, either... I mean, removing them from your dice pool entirely. If you presume they are the result of becoming Glamour-drunk and mentally unbalanced from too much Wyld magic, it seems gaining temporary Banality <i>should</i> be enough to offset them -- but I'm sure the game designers wanted to make a botch a bit more onerous than just a backfired cantrip. <br /> <br /> After all, if characters can reduce permanent Banality from time spent in the Dreaming or Quests undertaken (not easy, but possible), then there must be a way to get rid of that (permanent?) cursed dice in your pool, waiting to drag your character down with every roll. But if there is, I'm not finding it. Help?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24663-observer","name":"Observer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T12:10:26-07:00","id":1453065,"title":"","content":"Page 295, bottom of the page. Whenever you go through any method of Epiphany [aka gaining glamor from mortals] you can forgo a point of glamor to remove a point of Imbalanced Willpower. So you can\u2019t remove nightmare dice until you\u2019ve fully loaded up on them, but then you can remove the imbalanced willpower you get from them so there is a counter method. <br /> <br /> And outside of being the way to gain imbalanced willpower nightmare dice don\u2019t do anything harmful unless im forgetting something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26817-biapolis","name":"biapolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-21T12:38:11-07:00","id":1453068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>biapolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1451793-can-t-find-reference-any-way-to-get-rid-of-nightmare-dice-in-c20?p=1453065#post1453065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And outside of being the way to gain imbalanced willpower nightmare dice don\u2019t do anything harmful unless im forgetting something?</div> </div> </div> </div>They make it harder to control an unleashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-22T14:58:30-07:00","id":1453209,"title":"","content":"Oh, fair! That is unfortunate, but as far as I can tell you can only remove nightmare dice by filling up on them, and then cleaning the point of imbalanced willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26817-biapolis","name":"biapolis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T20:16:11-07:00","id":1453886,"title":"","content":"Ahh! Thank you both! I'd missed that completely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24663-observer","name":"Observer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T06:06:59-07:00","id":1453926,"title":"","content":"I'd probably rule that you can lose 1-3 at the end of a character defining quest. You might be able to loot 2e for some ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T18:52:15-07:00","id":1457535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>biapolis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1451793-can-t-find-reference-any-way-to-get-rid-of-nightmare-dice-in-c20?p=1453065#post1453065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you can forgo a point of glamor</div> </div> </div> </div>Just re-read, not quite. You don't forgo a point, you forgo the <i>entire</i> gain of glamour for that Epiphany.<br /> <br /> Outside that, I don't see the process as a big problem. Unleashing is an extremely powerful option by itself and even out of control is very interesting. I'm not against letting a character try to remove dice by means of any process you consider a good treatment for Bedlam, as long as the process is involving enough to make things interesting for the game or have a cost of sorts. But I don't think this is hugely needed either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}